cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "minevent: Minimal Event System for Machine Learning"
authors:
  - family-names: "Durand"
    given-names: "Thibaut"
    email: "durand.tibo+gh@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/durandtibo/minevent"
url: "https://durandtibo.github.io/minevent/"
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - event
  - event system
  - event handler
  - machine learning
  - python
abstract: >
  minevent is a Python library that provides a minimal event system
  for Machine Learning. It allows you to customize code by adding
  pieces of code that are executed when an event is fired. minevent
  is organized around three main concepts: event (a string that names
  something that happens), event handler (the callable to execute
  when the event happens), and event manager (which stores the event
  handlers and triggers the events).
